    /// row in the SAME transaction (design doc #7).
    /// `team_id`/`actor_user_id`/`target_user_id`/`old_role` carry no
    /// authorization weight here — the caller has already checked them —
    /// they exist purely to shape the audit row. Returns the number of
    /// `team_members` rows updated (0 or 1); the event is written only when
    /// that is 1, so a stale/already-departed `member_id` never produces a
    /// phantom audit entry.
    ///
    /// `action` (team-ocean lifecycle management, workspace-leave item):
    /// `'removed'` when an admin acted on someone else, `'left'` when the
    /// caller removed THEMSELVES (`routes::teams::remove_team_member` now
    /// permits `target_user_id == actor_user_id` without team-admin/org-admin
