    // ── RLS-scoped transaction surface: chunk 2 cluster ─────────────────────────
    // (org-tenancy rollout, PR B.0 chunk 2 — conversations/meetings/query-history/
    // activity/teams/node-relationship/op_log/coding-sessions. See the chunk 1
    // block above for the full design rationale — same mechanism, same
    // byte-identical-SQL-with-caller-supplied-tx pattern, same "no local
    // commit/rollback" rule, same default-Err fallback.)
    //
    // Left out of BOTH this chunk and chunk 1 (tracked as chunk 3 / follow-up
    // work, not this PR): `link_node_atom`, `merge_nodes`, `unmerge_nodes`,
    // `promote_node`, `ocean_stats` (chunk 1's original tangled five) plus
    // `batch_apply_remote_ops` (op_log's sync-replay engine — already uses
    // per-op SAVEPOINTs internally per review H11f, and is exactly as
    // tangled as the original five: composing it correctly under a shared
    // caller-owned transaction needs the same dedicated design pass, not a
    // mechanical port).
    //
    // Also out of scope for this "Store scoped-transaction surface" effort
    // entirely (not a gap in this PR — there is simply no `Store` trait
    // method to give a `_scoped` twin to): `oauth_tokens`, `slack_integrations`,
    // `slack_huddle_captures`, `outlook_watched_conversations`,
    // `outlook_workflows`, `teams_watched_resources`, `graph_subscriptions`,
    // `llm_usage`, `mcp_tool_calls`, and `queries` are read/written via direct
    // ad hoc SQL in `connectors/`, `routes/`, `workers/`, `llm/usage.rs`, and
    // `mcp/audit.rs` — never through `Store` — so RLS-scoping THEM requires
    // adding scoped-transaction variants to THOSE modules directly, a
    // different (and differently-owned) piece of work, not an extension of
    // this trait. `non_supersession_pair` USED TO have RLS enabled but no
    // reader/writer anywhere in the Rust codebase (dormant/reserved table) —
    // D3/§3.7 wired it (`is_non_supersession_pair[_scoped]`/
    // `mark_non_supersession_pair[_scoped]`, immediately above the
    // relationship-edges section of this trait), so it now has both.
    // `node_promotions` has no standalone `Store` method either; its
    // only access is inside `promote_node` (chunk 3).

