    // ── Journal TIER rollups (Today-journal ticket 15; migration
    //    0117/0028) — day/week/month, chained map-reduce off the hour tier.
    //    Postgres-plane only, same restriction as the rest of this section.
    //    Each method below has an unscoped (org-tenant) form and a `_scoped`
    //    (consumer-plane, per-account) sibling, mirroring EXACTLY the split
    //    `Store::journal_dirty_hours`/`_scoped` and
    //    `Store::upsert_journal_rollup`/`_scoped` already established for the
    //    hour tier — see `workers::journal_sweep`'s module doc
    //    ("Consumer-plane RLS scoping") for why an unscoped call hard-errors
    //    on the consumer plane and why this split exists at all.

    /// Insert (or, on a natural-key conflict, refresh) one day/week/month
    /// compiled tier row. The conflict target is `journal_rollups`' 4-column
