    /// resolved-tz produced a DIFFERENT `period_start` for what is, in local
    /// wall-clock terms, the same period — e.g. a day compiled once under
    /// the UTC fallback, then again under a just-captured `America/Chicago`,
    /// leaves the UTC-boundary row behind unless something deletes it: the
    /// natural key above never matches, since `period_start` itself moved).
    /// Deleted in the SAME transaction as the insert/update below, so a read
    /// can never observe both the old- and new-boundary row for one instant.
