    /// Acquire `SELECT 1 FROM teams WHERE id = $1 FOR UPDATE` for the
    /// duration of the caller's transaction — closes the last-admin race in
    /// `remove_team_member` (org-team-membership design doc #9/defect #1:
    /// `count_team_admins` read unlocked at READ COMMITTED let two
    /// concurrent removals of the two remaining admins both pass the guard
    /// and orphan the team). Called as the FIRST statement of every
    /// interactive membership write's scoped transaction
    /// (`add_member`/`remove_team_member`/the role-assignment PATCH), so
    /// every later read in that same transaction (admin counts, active-
    /// member lookups) is serialized against any concurrent writer on the
    /// same team.
    ///
    /// Deliberately NOT a DB constraint or trigger enforcing "a team always
    /// has an admin" — see the design doc's "Rejected, and why": the org
    /// offboard cascade (a different agent's work, out of this file's
    /// scope) must be allowed to orphan a team when its sole admin leaves
    /// the company, and a constraint would wedge that worker forever. This
    /// is purely a concurrency fence around the APPLICATION-level guard, not
    /// a new invariant.
    ///
    /// No unscoped counterpart: the race this closes is a
    /// concurrent-TRANSACTION phenomenon that only exists inside a real
    /// database transaction with row-level locking. Returns `false` if the team row does not
    /// exist (caller should 404).
